id: pm-jev-6fs0
title: Update triage and link backlog tests for typed host lookup refusals on the pinned toolchain
description: "The pm-toolchain Dependabot bump pins @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.10.28, whose GH-1613 change preserves typed PmClient lookup refusals: reading or mutating an item whose document is missing from disk now fails with the host code item_not_found instead of an unclassified error. The batch triage and link backlog tests asserted the old generic fallback reasons (jev_triage_failure, jev_link_failure); the host-error retention they guard (outcome failed, exit code 1, no receipts applied) is unchanged, and the rows now carry the more precise host code."
type: Chore
status: open
priority: 2
tags[4]: dependencies,"gh:unbraind/pm-jev#75",migration,sdk
created_at: "2026-11-03T09:59:09.226Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-03T10:27:36.926Z"
author: pi-toolchain-glm-1103
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-03T09:59:26.357Z",pi-toolchain-glm-1103,"Reproduced both failures locally: test/batch-triage.test.ts 'deleted and missing source documents...' expects jev_triage_failure for the missing-file case and test/link.test.ts 'link backlog preserves missing-source host failures...' expects jev_link_failure; both rows now report the host code item_not_found. Root cause: pm-cli 2026.10.28 GH-1613 preserves typed PmClient lookup refusals, so a missing item document surfaces item_not_found through the pm-jev error mapping instead of falling back to the generic decision-failure codes. Classification: test pinned old CLI behaviour; production code is correct (the host error is retained, receipts are not applied, exit code stays 1). Fix: assert item_not_found for the missing-document cases and document the upstream reference in a comment; keep every other assertion."
  "2026-11-03T10:27:13.958Z",pi-toolchain-glm-1103,"Evidence: node --test test/batch-triage.test.ts test/link.test.ts passes 28/28 (both previously failing tests included). Full suite npm test passes 398/398, plus typecheck and lint green. The merge from main took main's lockfile and @types/node 26.6.6 and kept the PR's pinned toolchain (@unbrained/pm-cli 2026.10.28, pm-changelog 2026.10.28, pm-ops 2026.10.29), re-resolved with a package-lock-only install. No production change was needed; the new typed refusal codes are an upstream improvement, recorded here for the review."
